WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.340
[intro music]

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.060
Okay, I'm gonna think about it this time

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.740
before I actually say it.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.500
Good morning, John, it's
Thursday, February 8th.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:20.480
It is.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.580
It's very hard to make a video blog in this house
because there's nowhere private at all,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.300
and I have to talk very quietly
or else people will look at me funny.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.100
They're looking at me funny.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.580
[high-pitched grunt]

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.960
I'm kind of hiding in the corner

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.180
in the living room,

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.580
which is the room that I sleep in,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.920
in a sofa bed,

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.280
which is right here.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.320
To start out today's video I'm
gonna give you a tour

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.020
of the place where I am right now.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.700
I am officially in Englewood, Florida.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.320
It's a very, very nice day.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.220
There's cars coming, which is really
unusual for this street.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.280
[car noise]

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.200
They would've hit me at the exact same time.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.980
That would've been painful.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.660
Yeah, see, now there's not gonna
be any cars for another 2 or 3 hours.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.260
And, you look around, you'll see

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:07.100
a normal Florida 50's-style
ranch house neighborhood.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.340
Very nice place.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.620
Lots of citrus,

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.960
lots of flowers and cacti,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.140
lots of American flags.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.740
This is a donkey with a cactus in it

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.420
that miraculously survived

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.420
Katherine throwing her calculus book at it.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.680
According to the sundial, it is 11:00.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.780
This is remarkably accurate.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.740
This mom has non-traditional pink flamingos.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.440
Behind me now

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.760
is an orange tree.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.520
Then over there

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.480
are two more orange trees and,
I think, a tangerine tree.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.660
And then I'm going underneath
some banana trees now,

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.780
and then there's the canal.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.640
It's a very nice place.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.840
Moving along.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.360
Katherine's parents just took me to a very

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.560
interesting

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:52.300
event.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.800
there were about 400 old people

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.240
watching about 30 old people

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.160
playing banjos.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.360
Badly.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.480
It turns out that Charlotte County has,
actually, the highest age of any county in the country.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.500
There are a lot

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.860
of old people here

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.280
They played patriotic songs,

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.360
they played "Take me out to the ball game",

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.120
they played

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.260
more

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.560
patriotic songs,

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.680
and they played some military songs.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:18.620
Anyways,

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.340
Whereas I've been thinking a
lot about babies lately,

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.440
you know, the beginning of life,

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.140
this made me think about something entirely different

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.560
I started to wonder,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.940
were any of them going to die

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.460
while I was watching them?

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.980
So, I've done some B.O.N. calculations,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.920
I love B.O.N. calculations,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.820
"Back of Napkin".

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.340
Assuming that the average age
of people there was 70,

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.260
and assuming that there were
around 400 people there,

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.220
and using census data that says that
the average age of death

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.520
of a 70-year-old is 83,

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.380
I have calculated the probability
that someone would die

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.080
at the event that I just attended.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.880
Because the average age of death
of a 70-year-old is 83,

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.260
half of the people

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.480
at the event

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:02.760
will be dead

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.500
in 13 years.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.020
That is 113,000 hours.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.680
Now, because I was at the event for 3 hours,

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.140
and there were 400 old people there,

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:11.920
that means

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.600
1,200 total old people hours.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.220
You put that number over the total half-life
of an old person at the age of 70,

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.060
and then divide by 2,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.380
and get a 0.53% chance that someone
would die within eye-shot of me

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.240
this afternoon.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.580
While that's not a very big number,

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.400
it is probably the biggest that number has ever been

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.300
in my life.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.220
So, now you know how bored I am.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.780
I accept your challenge and will answer my survey

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.800
The 3 minute and 30 second time limit is going
to be quite a barrier but I will do my best.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.280
and I very much enjoyed
your children's book

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.860
I'm considering doing the illustrations
for it myself.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.280
I'll see you tomorrow.

